huggins@dip.eecs.umich.edu (James K. Huggins), <2795@zipeecs.umich.edu>:
:One strategy (besides those mentioned) that I've found useful
:on low levels to deal with nymphs:
:
:You have to still have your pet with you for this to work.
: 
:First, drop all weapons, armor, etc.  (You may want to map out
:the entire level first to clear most of the native monsters.)
:[Involves running around the level for several hundred turns.]
     Lemme describe to you a smallish scenario, here, and show why this is
dangerous if not suicidal:

     Not too long ago I was running perhaps my most successful priest
(not all that big an honor; I died with a 12K score).  Level 8 and AC
-5.  Now, on dlvl 2 I discover, lo and behold, an unidentified scroll. 
Since I was wary of destroy armor scrolls and had some snazzy armor, I
removed all my armor.  (Might have left some of it on, but no big deal.)
The scroll turned out to be summon monster, and I was left with a nymph.
No big deal; I ran away.  Now, I manged to get a couple of squares away
and was walking thorugh a room when it suddenl started filling with
zombies.  Five of them.  I'm still unarmored.  Pisser.  But I'm armed
with my blessed dwarvish mattock, so I stand outside the room and start
killing them anyway.  (Only took one hit apiece.)  Great, except at that
moment a soldier ant (perhaps two; I didn't live long) decided to show
up after zombie #2 was dispatched.  Watching a soldier ant attack an AC
10 character is a pitiful sight; I lasted maybe three turns before it
did over 20hp damage (with poison) and killed my guy.  In retrospect, I
might have attempted an Elbereth to put my armor back on, but it would
have been a feeble hope.
     I had already cleaned out the level of monsters before attempting
this.  My character at the time had no intrinsics whatsoever, and his
luck was normal.  (Well, he had "stridently aligned.")
     Moral: Don't run around in the dungeon naked.  The monsters will
laugh at you.  (There's a rumor to that effect.)
     What I *should* have done was let the nymph steal something after
getting in a hit, and then put on my armor.  I took a big risk by
running around without armor and it didn't pay off.
     I also might have enscribed Elbereth with my fingers before trying
out the scroll, until discovering create monster scrolls.

